course: dictionary
lesson: 14291
title: Notional: an idea, not a real amount
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words name real things, and some name ideas. Notional is an idea word. It describes something that exists only as an estimate or a plan, not as a real or exact amount. «The class gave the sponsored walk a notional value of ten pounds, but no money was ever counted.» The ten pounds is a number used for planning or comparing, not money that changed hands.
explain: Use the context to check. Ask: is the sentence talking about real money or real things, or about a plan? In «The team set a notional budget of 500 pounds for the trip», the words set and budget show it is a planning number. Swap in a meaning, such as "an estimated number used for planning", and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Notional can also mean based on theory, not on facts or practice. «His notional idea of how bees fly was never tested.» Here the idea was only a theory. Notional is a formal word, so you will meet it most in maths, money and serious writing.
fact: Notional means existing only as an idea or estimate, not as something real or exact.
fact: Notional can also mean based on theory, not on facts or practice.
fact: A «notional sum» is a number used to compare or plan, not an amount anyone actually paid.
fact: Notional is a formal word, so it is more common in writing about money, maths and economics than in everyday talk.
fact: Clue words such as «estimate», «plan» and «budget» often sit near notional.
exercise: «The class gave the sponsored walk a notional value of ten pounds, but no money was ever counted.» What does notional mean here? | A very large sum of money | *An estimate used for planning, not real money | Money that was actually paid in full | A rare coin from long ago
exercise: «His notional idea of how bees fly was never tested.» What does the word notional suggest? | Proven by many experiments | Written in a foreign language | Funny and silly | *Based on theory, not on tested facts
exercise: «The team set a notional budget of 500 pounds to plan the trip.» Find and copy one word that signals a plan or estimate. | *budget | trip | pounds | team
test: «The shop gave the old tent a notional price of twenty pounds, but nobody bought it.» Which word is closest in meaning to notional? | Final | *Estimated | Real | Exact
test: Which sentence uses notional correctly? | She paid a notional ten pounds for the bag and took it home. | *The class used a notional price of one pound per apple to practise sums. | The bridge is notional, so you can walk across it today. | The notional river flooded my house last night.
exam: Ravi reads «a notional sum of 50 pounds» in a maths book. What is the best way to check what notional means? | Look it up in a book about birds | Ignore the word and skip the whole sentence | Assume it means very large | *Look for clues about planning or estimating, then swap in estimated and see if it fits
